.TH CHM-RESOURCE-MANAGER 1
.SH NAME
chm-resource-manager \\- opportunistic background resource governor
.SH DESCRIPTION
Monitors CPU, memory and I/O pressure and reduces background work when interactive workloads are under pressure. When pressure is low, background jobs may use additional capacity. It does not reserve or consume all resources continuously.
.SH STATE
Writes resource state to /run/chimera/resource.state by default.
